Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='opensweep', at=datetime(2026, 9, 21, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title="The open list is swept once a day by proposal, from mail after each todo's creation", body="*The open list is swept, by proposal* (2026-09-21, `docs/OPENSWEEP-PLAN-2026-09-21.md`; `secretary::sweep` and its `candidates`). Evidence that closes a todo rarely names its id (an airline's receipt never says `todo:life/flightcheckin`). So once a day after `review` the secretary walks the open list: for each todo, mail AFTER its `created` (or its latest trusted reopen, which stands until newer mail arrives) in the same thread, from the same sender, or naming its referents (a code, a flight, a person) — never its id, never its age — is laid before the model, whose ONLY write is `propose_changes` of `complete`/`cancel` with a `why` and the `mail:` that proves it; any other act, or a todo not shown that round, is refused before storage. The owner taps it in the Inbox. A todo with no later mail produces nothing: absence of evidence is not evidence.", rationale='Decided 2026-09-21 (docs/OPENSWEEP-PLAN-2026-09-21.md).', supersedes=()))